## 2. The proposal's four Aims

| Aim | Name | Status |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Discovery — SAEs, Feature Interpretability Score, concept probes | **NOT STARTED** |
| 2 | Mechanism — knock-out / injection, ACE, negative controls | **NOT STARTED** |
| 3 | Control — Constraint-Aware Layer, `h'_l = h_l + α·P_causal(h_l)` | **PROXY ONLY** — current gate is post-hoc, not a residual-stream adapter |
| 4 | Validation — counterfactual benchmark, uncertainty-aware deferral | **MOSTLY DONE** — one component (UQ) failed and is documented as a negative result |

Research questions:

| RQ | Question | Status |
|---|---|---|
| RQ1 | Sparse latent features → biomedical concepts with semantic coherence | **NOT ADDRESSED** — requires Aim 1 |
| RQ2 | Targeted interventions → predictable causally consistent changes | **NOT ADDRESSED** — requires Aim 2 |
| RQ3 | Symbolic constraints improve consistency without harming language ability | **HALF** — consistency improvement shown (0.281→0.641); the language-capability control has not been run (`src/perplexity.py` written but never executed) |

Everything built so far is behavioural. No model activations have been touched.

---

## 3. DONE

### Infrastructure
- 12 modules under `src/`: dataset construction, model wrapper, RAG + symbolic
  gate, metrics and statistics, eval driver, table generator, two diagnostics.
- BioMistral-7B in bf16, greedy decoding, single GPU. No quantisation.
- `MockLM` backend for GPU-free plumbing checks, with a warning banner in
  `make_table.py` so mock numbers can never be reported by accident.

### Benchmark
- 10 contraindication rule families — 8 training, 2 held out
  (`nitrofurantoin_renal`, `ondansetron_qt`).
- `counterfactual_test.jsonl` 128 records / 64 pairs; `_heldout` 32 / 16;
  `_calib` 32 / 16; `rag_corpus.jsonl` 22 passages.
- Each pair flips exactly one causal variable across a threshold, so the label
  flip is guaranteed. Ground truth generated programmatically — no LLM-as-judge,
  no human annotation.
- `hardening.py`: near-threshold values, indirect presentation of the causal
  factor in half the templates, 3 distractor labs per case. Applied after an
  initial saturated result — legitimate but **must be disclosed**.

### Results
- Full 4-variant ablation on test and held-out splits.
- Paired McNemar with Holm correction across the three consecutive comparisons.
- Arm-wise breakdown exposing the base model's over-caution
  (UNSAFE arm 0.891 / SAFE arm 0.297).
- Symbolic gate fires on 72/128 and makes 0 incorrect decisions when it fires.

### Closed investigations
- **P3 retrieval** (`results/p3_retrieval.md`) — hit@3 = 0.648 test, 1.000
  held-out. Retrieval works; the model ignores the retrieved context. "RAG is
  insufficient on this benchmark" is now defensible.
- **P1 uncertainty signals** (`results/p1_uq_signals.md`) — entropy has no
  signal on any population. `logit_margin` is reliably better than entropy
  (+0.199 base, p=0.004), but no signal clears the bar on the population the UQ
  engine actually governs. Negative result confirmed, one positive finding kept.

### Bugs found and fixed
Four, all documented in `HANDOFF.md` §5 with instructions not to reintroduce
them, plus the SPM tokenizer trap that cost one discarded eval run.

### Data acquisition
- `fetch_openfda.py` run against the live API. `data/openfda_raw.jsonl`
  (10 labels) and `data/curation_worksheet.csv` (145 rows, 82 containing a
  number).

